diff --git a/docs/models/mimir2.md b/docs/models/mimir2.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..00108750c0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/models/mimir2.md
@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@
+# Mimir2
+
+This local integration serves converted HRM-Text-v2 checkpoints with architecture
+`Mimir2ForCausalLM`. It requires the companion Transformers checkout that defines
+`Mimir2Config`; upstream published Transformers releases do not yet provide it.
+No remote checkpoint is claimed by the model test registry.
+
+## Supported semantics
+
+- Default features reproduce HRM-Text's H/L recurrence.
+- Per-invocation input-dependent gates load their saved alpha and parameters.
+- Top-k MLP mixtures use dense reference execution, even when the training
+  configuration says `moe_sparse`. This preserves the selected mixture but does
+  not promise sparse inference speedups.
+- Dense mixtures of L stacks support shared or separate recurrent states.
+- Sparse MoS supports first-token and PrefixLM prefix-mean routing with either
+  state mode. Routes are reconstructed from original request prompts, including
+  after scheduler reordering/preemption. Selected projections/MLPs execute
+  sparsely; attention still uses full-batch metadata and KV allocation. This is
+  not a k/n reduction in attention cost or cache memory. Prefix-mean routing
+  currently re-embeds the prompt each decode step.
+- Residual branches, input-dependent residual mixing, and H/L memory branches
+  reuse the cache-independent mathematical helpers from Transformers.
+- Every expert and recurrent attention invocation has a distinct KV-cache slot.
+- Split HF G/Q/K/V and gate/up weights are packed in their original order.
+  Incomplete, duplicate or mixed packed/split projections are rejected. Required
+  feature buffers are checked as well as parameters.
+
+PrefixLM means the entire submitted prompt is bidirectional, followed by causal
+single-token decoding. This is **not** equivalent to ordinary causal prefill or
+to an arbitrary mixed prefix/response mask. Compare against HF with prompt
+`token_type_ids=1`. Prefix caching and chunked prefill must remain disabled;
+vLLM also detects the non-causal attention cache and disables these globally.
+The causal configuration (`prefix_lm=false`) uses normal vLLM attention.
+
+## Explicit limitations
+
+N-gram memory supports independently hashed split-width heads and the native
+contextual sigmoid gate. The worker stages bounded windows from request-owned
+token records in stable graph buffers. Use `async_scheduling=False` (CLI:
+`--no-async-scheduling`). Async scheduling, prompt embeddings and dual batch
+overlap are explicitly rejected for n-grams. CPU request isolation, strict
+weights and fullgraph feature math are tested; n-gram CUDA engine logits and
+graph replay remain unmeasured because all GPUs were occupied. This is an
+Engram-inspired variant, not an exact Qwen reproduction.
+Sparse MoS requires `--enforce-eager`. Speculative decoding, pipeline parallelism
+and quantized loading are rejected. Tensor-parallel primitives are used, but multi-GPU serving
+has not been qualified. CUDA graphs/compilation need separate qualification.
+This integration does not replace the production environment or exports.
+
+## Local environment and checks
+
+The development conda environment is `mimir2`, not `hrm2`. Source checkouts:
+
+- `$MIMIR_DEPS/transformers`, branch `mimir2`.
+- `$MIMIR_DEPS/vllm`, branch `mimir2`, based on
+  `a46abb7ae68acc13a4fc5870db98619b3f97c6e0` (the production-known vLLM revision).
+
+Dependencies are installed with `uv pip`. The editable vLLM installation uses
+matching precompiled binaries, not a production environment clone:
+
+```bash
+conda activate mimir2
+VLLM_USE_PRECOMPILED=1 \
+VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_COMMIT=a46abb7ae68acc13a4fc5870db98619b3f97c6e0 \
+VLLM_PRECOMPILED_WHEEL_VARIANT=cu132 \
+uv pip install --no-build-isolation -e $MIMIR_DEPS/vllm -e $MIMIR_DEPS/transformers
+
+python tests/models/language/generation/test_mimir2_contracts.py
+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 VLLM_ENABLE_V1_MULTIPROCESSING=0 \
+  python examples/offline_inference/mimir2_parity.py
+# Repeat with --features and/or --causal.
+# Prepared, NOT GPU-qualified: --ngram --compiled --dtype bfloat16.
+# --features --dtype bfloat16 checks the reduced-precision serving path.
+```
+
+CUDA 13.2 is installed through conda in this environment. Its saved activation
+variables set `CUDA_HOME` to the environment prefix and
+`FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE=$MIMIR_DEPS/vllm/.runtime-cache`. The pip compiler bundle
+resolved mixed compiler/header versions and failed FlashInfer compilation; use
+the conda toolkit, not `site-packages/nvidia/cu13`, as `CUDA_HOME`.
+
+The smoke uses tiny synthetic weights, a 64 MiB KV allocation, two short
+requests, and three generated tokens per request. It compares greedy IDs and
+log probabilities with HF, without W&B. It is not a full-size benchmark.
+Validated locally: FP32 default and combined-feature PrefixLM, FP32
+combined-feature causal, and BF16 combined-feature PrefixLM. The October 20 contextual-memory extension has nine passing CPU contracts;
+the companion Transformers suite has fifteen passing test methods. These CPU
+results do not extend the preceding GPU qualification to n-grams.
+
+For a real checkpoint, start conservatively with eager execution, a memory
+budget appropriate to the free GPU, and the exported tokenizer's chat template:
+
+```bash
+vllm serve /path/to/mimir2-export --enforce-eager \
+  --no-enable-prefix-caching --no-enable-chunked-prefill
+```
+
+Do not copy the tiny smoke's memory settings for a production checkpoint.
diff --git a/examples/offline_inference/mimir2_parity.py b/examples/offline_inference/mimir2_parity.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..f4feab8108
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/offline_inference/mimir2_parity.py
@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
+"""Tiny loaded-weight HF/vLLM parity, no downloaded models or logging services."""
+
+import argparse
+import tempfile
+
+import torch
+from transformers import Mimir2Config, Mimir2ForCausalLM
+
+from vllm import LLM, SamplingParams
+
+
+def main():
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()
+    parser.add_argument("--ngram", action="store_true")
+    parser.add_argument("--features", action="store_true")
+    parser.add_argument("--causal", action="store_true")
+    parser.add_argument("--sparse", action="store_true")
+    parser.add_argument(
+        "--compiled",
+        action="store_true",
+        help="Enable normal vLLM compilation and CUDA graphs",
+    )
+    parser.add_argument(
+        "--routing", choices=("first_token", "prefix_mean"), default="first_token"
+    )
+    parser.add_argument("--active", type=int, default=1)
+    parser.add_argument("--state", choices=("shared", "separate"), default="shared")
+    parser.add_argument("--dtype", choices=("float32", "bfloat16"), default="float32")
+    args = parser.parse_args()
+    torch.manual_seed(17)
+    features = (
+        dict(
+            gates_enabled=True,
+            gate_alpha=0.7,
+            moe_num_experts=2,
+            moe_top_k=1,
+            moe_sparse=True,
+            moe_levels="both",
+            mos_num_experts=2,
+            mos_top_k=2,
+            mos_state_mode="separate",
+            residual_branches=2,
+            residual_input_dependent=True,
+            residual_alpha=0.6,
+            h_memory_branches=2,
+            memory_alpha=0.5,
+        )
+        if args.features
+        else {}
+    )
+    if args.sparse:
+        features.update(
+            mos_num_experts=3,
+            mos_top_k=args.active,
+            mos_sparse=True,
+            mos_sparse_routing=args.routing,
+            mos_state_mode=args.state,
+        )
+    if args.ngram:
+        features.update(
+            ngram_orders=[2, 3],
+            ngram_heads=4,
+            ngram_contextual_gate=True,
+            ngram_buckets=31,
+            ngram_alpha=0.7,
+        )
+    config = Mimir2Config(
+        vocab_size=128,
+        hidden_size=64,
+        intermediate_size=128,
+        num_hidden_layers=1,
+        num_attention_heads=2,
+        head_dim=32,
+        max_position_embeddings=64,
+        embedding_scale=1.0,
+        prefix_lm=not args.causal,
+        eos_token_id=None,
+        pad_token_id=0,
+        **features,
+    )
+    config._attn_implementation = "sdpa"
+    model = Mimir2ForCausalLM(config).eval()
+    with torch.no_grad():
+        for name, value in model.named_parameters():
+            if any(
+                key in name
+                for key in (
+                    "invocation_gates",
+                    "read_gain",
+                    "rows.",
+                    "biases.",
+                    "ngram.tables",
+                )
+            ):
+                value.normal_(std=0.07)
+    model.to(getattr(torch, args.dtype))
+    prompts = [[1, 2, 3, 4], [9, 8, 7]]
+    expected = []
+    with torch.no_grad():
+        for prompt in prompts:
+            tokens, generated, logprobs = list(prompt), [], []
+            for _ in range(3):
+                ids = torch.tensor([tokens])
+                types = torch.tensor([[1] * len(prompt) + [0] * len(generated)])
+                logits = model(ids, token_type_ids=types, use_cache=False).logits[0, -1]
+                token = logits.argmax().item()
+                logprobs.append(logits.float().log_softmax(-1)[token].item())
+                generated.append(token)
+                tokens.append(token)
+            expected.append((generated, logprobs))
+    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="mimir2-parity-") as folder:
+        model.save_pretrained(folder)
+        engine = LLM(
+            model=folder,
+            skip_tokenizer_init=True,
+            dtype=args.dtype,
+            enforce_eager=not args.compiled,
+            max_model_len=64,
+            max_num_seqs=2,
+            max_num_batched_tokens=64,
+            gpu_memory_utilization=0.02,
+            kv_cache_memory_bytes=64 * 1024 * 1024,
+            async_scheduling=False,
+            enable_prefix_caching=False,
+            enable_chunked_prefill=False,
+        )
+        outputs = engine.generate(
+            [{"prompt_token_ids": ids} for ids in prompts],
+            SamplingParams(temperature=0, max_tokens=3, ignore_eos=True, logprobs=1),
+            use_tqdm=False,
+        )
+        for result, (tokens, probs) in zip(outputs, expected):
+            output = result.outputs[0]
+            assert list(output.token_ids) == tokens, (output.token_ids, tokens)
+            actual = [p[t].logprob for p, t in zip(output.logprobs, tokens)]
+            tolerance = 2e-3 if args.dtype == "float32" else 3e-2
+            torch.testing.assert_close(
+                torch.tensor(actual),
+                torch.tensor(probs),
+                atol=tolerance,
+                rtol=tolerance,
+            )
+        print(
+            f"PASS: features={args.features} sparse={args.sparse} "
+            f"ngram={args.ngram} routing={args.routing} active={args.active} "
+            f"state={args.state} causal={args.causal} dtype={args.dtype}; "
+            "prefill + 3 decode tokens, two requests"
+        )
+        engine.llm_engine.engine_core.shutdown()
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()
